                <pb facs="0666" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg558"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal of Her Majesty’s Government for a modus
                        vivendi in the Behring Sea during the present fishing season</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received June 4.)</dateline></opener>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>The Government of Great Britain and of the United States shall prohibit
                        until May, 1892, the killing of seals in Behring Sea or any <pb facs="0667"
                            n="559" xml:id="pg559"/> islands thereof, and will, to the best of their
                        power and ability, insure that subjects and citizens of the two nations,
                        respectively, and the vessels flying their respective flags shall observe
                        that prohibition.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>During the period above specified the United States Government shall have
                        the right to kill 7,500 seals.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Consuls may at any time be appointed to the islands in the Behring Sea,
                        and the United States Government will grant an “exequatur” to any such
                        consuls.</item>
                    <label>(4)</label>
                    <item>Unless the assent of Russia be obtained to this convention, it shall not
                        come into operation.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
